                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07a28d4a-0993-4831-8251-179cab6dcf97",
                                                "sense_id": "3dcfb582-6006-3edc-9d2a-27e6c249fa08",
                                                "text": "Many future prime ministers were schooled in Eton."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "134da4ae-243e-4738-a29b-a1dc7003c68d",
                                                "sense_id": "3dcfb582-6006-3edc-9d2a-27e6c249fa08",
                                                "text": "I tooke delights / In plucking Apples from t’Heſperian Trees, / Which Eating, I grew Learn’d: adde to All theſe / My Priuate Readings, which more School’d my Soule, / Then Tutors, when they ſternliest did Controll / With Frownes or Rods: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "647eac7b-545b-35af-bba4-2ed8241aecac",
                                        "entry_id": "797e5bad-a99b-3c25-b3c3-44c0f1d6e97e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To defeat emphatically, to teach an opponent a harsh lesson."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fd0a099-b107-4ea1-a85c-0c75d0bd5ac0",
                                                "sense_id": "647eac7b-545b-35af-bba4-2ed8241aecac",
                                                "text": "A blind law graduate who put the National Conference of Bar Examiners to the test got schooled in federal court."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d61678b7-005e-476f-bcea-1d315e8ff4bd",
                                                "sense_id": "647eac7b-545b-35af-bba4-2ed8241aecac",
                                                "text": "Two weeks later, the Cornhuskers put on their road whites again and promptly got schooled by miserable Iowa State in Ames. After the shocking loss […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a44f6ec0-f8e7-4358-8860-8d7bfc3ba301",
                                                "sense_id": "647eac7b-545b-35af-bba4-2ed8241aecac",
                                                "text": "\"You again?\" Sandman demanded. \"I guess you didn't learn your lesson.\"\n\"This time I'm gonna school you.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a25272f-b5e5-46b3-b6ca-906149e1946e",
                                                "sense_id": "647eac7b-545b-35af-bba4-2ed8241aecac",
                                                "text": "Mr. Harris said he was confident he could go toe to toe with any skeptic; he bragged that he’d recently schooled some crypto haters from Vice News."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa76b21f-5558-3c6b-a9a0-33c46d8fe1c9",
                                        "entry_id": "797e5bad-a99b-3c25-b3c3-44c0f1d6e97e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To control, or compose, one’s expression."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7a1e6c0-16f7-4a88-8bf9-2fe8aada9611",
                                                "sense_id": "fa76b21f-5558-3c6b-a9a0-33c46d8fe1c9",
                                                "text": "She took care to school her expression, not giving away any of her feelings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
